  "_comment": [
    "Cards for the clue-giving game: one person describes the concept, their",
    "team guesses it, and the four forbidden words are the ones that would end",
    "the round in a sentence. The concept itself is always forbidden, so it is",
    "never listed.",
    "",
    "Two rules held while writing these. The forbidden words are the *obvious*",
    "ones, not the clever ones — taking away the four words a person would",
    "actually reach for is what makes the game, while taking away an obscure",
    "synonym only makes it feel unfair. And every concept is something a group",
    "can picture: people, places, events and objects, never doctrines. 'Grace'",
    "is a fine sermon and a terrible clue.",
    "",
    "Difficulty is how obscure the concept is, not how hard it is to describe."
  ],
